From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0334-frizti-04-compute-same-value-writes-not-sent.patch

Source: 0334-frizti-04-compute-same-value-writes-not-sent.patch
kepler_compute: plain writes that keep a register's value stay on the front (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone, and with frizti-01 in either order.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 516ba08ce5, 4ddc1a058d, 763f3abbc0 (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166) and 5c173ca274
(Frizti), GPL-3.0-or-later.

EDEN_NX2_COMPUTE_SAME=1. Macros replay the QMD fields for every dispatch. Each write is a ring entry
and a call on the back that stores a word, mostly the word already there. With the switch the front
drops those, for plain registers it has sent once. Both threads do less. No number from the source.

Also under the switch: the front's copy of 0xb0 follows an inline QMD launch, as on the back. And
EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY=1 compares the front's compute registers with the back's every 4096 macro calls
and logs differences. Use it for the first run. Only "Split front compute register" lines judge this
switch: the same variable turns on the 3D check, which has its own lines.

Changed from the source: only the drop. Its tagged sink entries and ring pairs are left out, they
would touch the ring's format for less. The switch is read when the front starts, as Frizti fixed.
Verify skips code_loc, see below, which the source would report as a false difference.

Runs on the PS5: yes, with macros on the first thread, which is what run 61 logs.
Hang: no wait added. A wrong drop would leave a stale QMD field and a wrong dispatch. By the code only
the plain path writes these registers on the back, with one exception: DispatchNativeCompute sets
regs.code_loc from the QMD before every use, so a dropped write there changes nothing.
Pool memory: none (448 bytes per compute engine).
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile. Not run. Verify's comparison has never run either.

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
index 3d02011a41..b8572f132e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -1267,8 +1267,37 @@ struct KeplerCompute::FrontState {
     bool compute_uploaded{};
     u32 bind_pointer{};
     MacroEngine* macro{}; ///< Without a native context: the one macro engine
+    bool drop_same{};     ///< EDEN_NX2_COMPUTE_SAME, read once
+    /// Plain registers (native_plain_methods) this front sent a write to: the back stored the value
+    /// in both native_registers and regs, so `registers` holds what both hold.
+    std::bitset<0xe00> plain_sent;
+    u64 calls{}; ///< Macro calls, for EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY
 };
 
+namespace {
+
+// EDEN_NX2_COMPUTE_SAME=1: a plain compute register write that keeps the register's value is not
+// sent to the back. Macros replay the QMD fields for every dispatch, and each one was a ring entry
+// and a CallMethod that stores the same word. Only plain registers: nothing but that store happens
+// on the back, and only the plain path writes them there. With EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY set, the
+// front's copy is compared with the back's every 4096 macro calls.
+// From Frizti/Lichii 516ba08ce5 and 4ddc1a058d (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166), compute part, without
+// its tagged sink entries. Read when the front starts: env.txt is applied in main.
+bool ComputeDropSame() {
+    static const bool drop = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_COMPUTE_SAME");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return drop;
+}
+
+bool ComputeFrontVerify() {
+    static const bool verify = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY") != nullptr;
+    return verify;
+}
+
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 KeplerCompute::FrontState& KeplerCompute::Front(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split) {
     if (!front) [[unlikely]] {
         // Copy the back's state and take the macros over while it is idle.
@@ -1282,6 +1311,7 @@ KeplerCompute::FrontState& KeplerCompute::Front(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split) {
         front->compute_uploaded = native_compute_uploaded;
         front->bind_pointer = native_bind_pointer;
         front->macro = native_macro;
+        front->drop_same = ComputeDropSame();
         front_macros = true;
     }
     return *front;
@@ -1294,6 +1324,20 @@ void KeplerCompute::FrontApply(FrontState& fs, u32 method, u32 argument) {
     }
     fs.registers[method] = argument;
     switch (method) {
+    case 0x107:
+        // An inline QMD whose destination is mapped launches through ProcessNativeMethod(0xb0, 3)
+        // on the back, which leaves 3 in 0xb0 (0xad is restored). From Frizti/Lichii 763f3abbc0
+        // (Dr. Sergio) and 5c173ca274 (Frizti). Here only with the switch on.
+        if (fs.drop_same) {
+            const GPUVAddr address =
+                ((GPUVAddr{fs.registers[0xc6]} << 32) | fs.registers[0xc7]) << 8;
+            const u32 control = fs.registers[0xa7];
+            if (memory_manager.IsFullyMappedRange(address, 256) &&
+                ((control & (1U << 24)) || !(fs.registers[0xcc] & (1U << 12)))) {
+                fs.registers[0xb0] = 3;
+            }
+        }
+        break;
     case 0x45:
         FrontMacroEngine(fs).ClearCode(argument);
         break;
@@ -1354,10 +1398,54 @@ void KeplerCompute::FrontCallMethod(Core::System& system, VideoCommon::GpuSplit&
         }
         return;
     }
+    if (FrontDropsWrite(fs, method, argument)) {
+        return;
+    }
     FrontApply(fs, method, argument);
     split.Method(this, method, argument, is_last_call, segment);
 }
 
+bool KeplerCompute::FrontDropsWrite(FrontState& fs, u32 method, u32 argument) {
+    if (!fs.drop_same || method >= native_plain_methods.size() || !native_plain_methods[method]) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (fs.plain_sent[method] && fs.registers[method] == argument) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    fs.plain_sent[method] = true;
+    return false;
+}
+
+void KeplerCompute::FrontVerify(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& fs) {
+    split.Drain();
+    static u64 checks{};
+    static u64 differences{};
+    ++checks;
+    for (u32 i = 0; i < 0xe00; ++i) {
+        // Dropped writes rely on regs holding what native_registers holds. Not code_loc:
+        // DispatchNativeCompute sets it in regs alone, from the QMD, before every use.
+        const bool code_loc = i == KEPLER_COMPUTE_REG_INDEX(code_loc.address_high) ||
+                              i == KEPLER_COMPUTE_REG_INDEX(code_loc.address_low);
+        const bool regs_differ = fs.plain_sent[i] && !code_loc && i < Regs::NUM_REGS &&
+                                 regs.reg_array[i] != native_registers[i];
+        if (fs.registers[i] == native_registers[i] && !regs_differ) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (differences++ < 64) {
+            LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "Split front compute register {:#x}: front {:#x}, back {:#x}{}", i,
+                        fs.registers[i], native_registers[i],
+                        regs_differ ? fmt::format(" (back regs {:#x})", regs.reg_array[i])
+                                    : std::string{});
+        }
+        fs.registers[i] = native_registers[i];
+        fs.plain_sent[i] = false;
+    }
+    if ((checks & 63) == 1) {
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Split front compute register checks: {} done, {} differences", checks,
+                 differences);
+    }
+}
+
 void KeplerCompute::FrontCallMultiMethod(Core::System& system, VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split,
                                          u32 method, const u32* base_start, u32 amount,
                                          u32 methods_pending, const GPUVAddr* segment) {
@@ -1400,6 +1488,9 @@ void KeplerCompute::FrontRunMacro(Core::System& system, VideoCommon::GpuSplit& s
             if (address >= 0xe00) {
                 return false;
             }
+            if (FrontDropsWrite(fs, address, value)) {
+                return true;
+            }
             FrontApply(fs, address, value);
             split.MacroWrite(this, address, value);
             return true;
@@ -1413,6 +1504,9 @@ void KeplerCompute::FrontRunMacro(Core::System& system, VideoCommon::GpuSplit& s
     fs.executing_macro.reset();
 #endif
     fs.parameters.clear();
+    if (fs.drop_same && ComputeFrontVerify() && (++fs.calls & 4095) == 0) [[unlikely]] {
+        FrontVerify(split, fs);
+    }
 }
 
 } // namespace Tegra::Engines
diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
index 5eeb03e3f3..eca391240f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.h
@@ -277,6 +277,8 @@ private:
     MacroEngine& FrontMacroEngine(FrontState& state);
     std::span<u32> FrontMacroPositions(FrontState& state);
     void FrontRunMacro(Core::System& system, VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& state);
+    bool FrontDropsWrite(FrontState& state, u32 method, u32 argument);
+    void FrontVerify(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& state);
     std::unique_ptr<FrontState> front;
     bool front_macros{}; ///< The front owns the macro code and bindings (the back skips them)
 
